<td id="A1.T5.2.20.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb"><math id="A1.T5.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.1</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We report how the scaled number of parameters is allocated across our models. We also indicate the number of Fourier frequencies encoded (see Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 4D Position Encoding Strategy ‣ 2 Methods ‣ REVE: A Foundation Model for EEG Adapting to Any Setup with Large-Scale Pretraining on 25,000 Subjects" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>). Note that no frequency truncation was required, as we closely matched the hidden dimension of our models to the number of components generated by the 4D PE module.</p>
</div>
