<div id="A3.SS6.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS6.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS6.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">HMC</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Alvarez-Estevez and Rijsman, 2021</a>)</cite>. The Haaglanden Medisch Centrum (HMC) Sleep Staging Database is a sleep stage detection dataset, consisting of 151 full-night polysomnographic (PSG) recordings collected from patients referred for sleep studies. The data includes EEG, EOG, EMG, and ECG channels, with a sampling rate of 256 Hz, and annotations for five sleep stages (Wake, N1, N2, N3, REM) manually scored by trained sleep technicians. HMC is under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International Public License.</p>
</div>
